  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Commonwealth Standards Network - Phase 5</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Commonwealth Standards Network (CSN) was launched in 2018 and has been managed by BSI since its inception; it has received four rounds of DFID/FCDO funding. Phase 5 of the programme will build on the previous Outputs and continue to engage the CSN stakeholders to act as a collaborative network with an influential international voice that supports the increased use of international standards in Commonwealth ODA-eligible countries &#x2013; primarily by strengthening the capacity of their National Standards Bodies (NSBs) so they can support their stakeholders (including Policy Makers and the Private Sector) to use international standards as tools to enhance trade and development and strengthen Regulatory alignment. It will also build on the wider work being funded by FCDO under the Standards Partnership Programme and complementing other relevant programmes such as the Commonwealth Investment Network.</narrative>
  </description>
